        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c596bd68-e998-52f3-81cb-d3bbfcae492b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Quonset Point, NAS Quonset Point, Camp Endicott, Davisville, North Kingstown, Rhode Island\n- Organizations: United States Navy, Naval Construction Battalions, Seabees, Davisville Naval Construction Battalion Center, National Register of Historic Places\n- Products: Quonset hut\n- Topics: World War II, military facilities, historic preservation\n\nFacts:\n- During World War II, Quonset Point gave its name to the Quonset hut, a standardized temporary structure used by the U.S. military.\n- Camp Endicott was a United States Navy Seabee facility that was part of the Davisville Naval Construction Battalion Center at Quonset Point in North Kingstown, Rhode Island.\n- Camp Endicott at Davisville was next to NAS Quonset Point and was the home of the Naval Construction Battalions known as the Seabees.\n- In 1978, a surviving portion of Camp Endicott, which was mostly demolished, was listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
